12
00:48:31,304 --> 00:48:37,304
Madagascar 3: Europe's Most Wanted is a 2012 American animated comedy film directed by Eric
Darnell, Conrad Vernon and Tom McGrath, and written by Darnell and Noah Baumbach.

13
00:52:33,913 --> 00:52:39,913
The third in the Madagascar film series, it was
produced by DreamWorks Animation.

14
00:56:36,521 --> 00:56:42,521
The film features Ben Stiller, Chris Rock, David Schwimmer, Jada Pinkett Smith, Sacha Baron Cohen, Cedric the Entertainer, Andy Richter, McGrath, Chris Miller, Christopher Knights,
John DiMaggio and Vernon reprising their roles from the previous films, with Jessica Chastain, Bryan Cranston, Martin Short and Frances McDormand joining the cast.

15
01:00:39,130 --> 01:00:45,130
In the film, the main characters—a party of animals from the Central Park Zoo whose adventures have already taken them to Madagascar and Africa—attempt to return to
New York City and find themselves traveling across Europe with a circus while being pursued by the villainous head of Monaco's animal control service.

16
01:04:41,739 --> 01:04:47,739
DreamWorks Animation announced the third film in August 2008,
three months before the release of the second film.

17
01:08:44,347 --> 01:08:50,347
As with the previous films in the franchise, the
score was composed by Hans Zimmer.

18
01:12:46,956 --> 01:12:52,956
Madagascar 3: Europe's Most Wanted premiered out of competition at the 2012 Cannes Film Festival on May 18,
2012, and was theatrically released in the United States on June 8 by Paramount Pictures.

19
01:16:49,565 --> 01:16:55,565
It received generally positive reviews and was the eighth highest-grossing film of
2012, with a gross of $746 million against a budget of $145 million.

20
01:20:52,173 --> 01:20:58,173
A spin-off, Penguins of Madagascar, was released in 2014.

21
01:24:54,782 --> 01:25:00,782
The film explores themes of friendship, circus, lion, zoo, hippopotamus.

22
01:28:57,391 --> 01:29:03,391
The tone is lighthearted.
